{"packet_id":"X002-01","doc_id":"X002","jurisdiction":"Jersey City, NJ","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Jersey City rent control annual allowable increase","requirement":"A landlord may not request or receive a rent increase greater than 4% or the percentage difference in the consumer price index, whichever is less, and only one increase is permitted in any 12-month period.","key_value":"4% or CPI difference, whichever is less","coverage_conditions":"Rent control covers dwellings with five or more housing spaces; dwellings with four or fewer housing spaces are exempt, but that exemption is suspended for non-owner-occupied small dwellings during the state of emergency.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"units","role":"exempt","op":"at_most","n":4},{"type":"other","text":"Newly constructed dwellings with 25 or more dwelling units in a City Council-approved redevelopment area are exempt"},{"type":"other","text":"Low rent public housing developments are exempt"},{"type":"other","text":"Buildings converted from nonpermanent dwelling use to dwelling use on or after October 1, 1983 are exempt"}],"per_tenancy":"A new dwelling or housing space rented for the first time is exempt for the initial rental only; the four-or-fewer-space exemption is suspended for non-owner-occupied dwellings while the state of emergency lasts.","coverage_quotes":["Dwellings with four or less housing spaces; provided, however, that this exemption shall be suspended for non-owner occupied dwellings with four or less housing spaces until the end of the state of emergency or six months from adoption of these amendments whichever comes first.","Newly constructed dwellings with 25 or more dwelling units located within a redevelopment area as defined in Section 5 of the Redevelopment Agencies Law, N.J.S.A. 40:55C-5(o), for which the City Council has approved a redevelopment plan","Low rent public housing developments."]},"exemptions":"Dwellings with four or fewer housing spaces; licensed hotels and motels; commercial and industrial space; newly constructed dwellings of 25 or more units in an approved redevelopment area; low-rent public housing; buildings converted to dwelling use on or after October 1, 1983.","penalty":"Any rental increase in excess of that authorized by this chapter is void, and excess rent must be refunded or credited by the landlord forthwith.","effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Jersey City Mun. Code § 260-3","quoted_span":"At the expiration of a lease or at the termination of a lease of a periodic tenant, no landlord of any dwelling as defined in § 260-1 may request or receive a percentage increase in rent which is greater than four percent or the percentage difference between the consumer price index three months prior to the expiration or termination of the lease and three months prior to the commencement of the lease term, whichever is less.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"X002-01","doc_id":"X002","jurisdiction":"Jersey City, NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Jersey City just cause for eviction standard","requirement":"The chapter defines 'just cause for eviction' as the landlord recovering possession of a housing space or dwelling for one of the reasons outlined in state law, N.J.S.A. 2A:18-53 as amended or N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1 et seq.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"This part of the chapter states only the definition and ties just cause to the grounds listed in state law; it states no separate coverage limits.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Jersey City Mun. Code § 260-1","quoted_span":"JUST CAUSE FOR EVICTION—That the landlord recovered possession of a housing space or dwelling for one of the reasons outlined in State law (N.J.S.A. 2A:18-53 as amended or N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1 et seq.).","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.5,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
